[{:db/id "q-350800/field-1/d8a60767af0b999302e1a0d0be555196209eba44113f15b9c44799eb67b9fe02" :answer/id #uuid "8d76b388-31ea-5593-ba50-2fbabd4cccd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7e^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350800/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac5b5429-d1e6-5907-92a4-fbe28584db05" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350800/field-1/d8a60767af0b999302e1a0d0be555196209eba44113f15b9c44799eb67b9fe02" :answer-field/choices ["q-350800/field-1/d8a60767af0b999302e1a0d0be555196209eba44113f15b9c44799eb67b9fe02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350800" :question/id #uuid "68bb759e-539a-555e-bba1-a116dee326cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-350800" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}7{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}7{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =7\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{x}]}_{a}^{-3} \\\\  & =7\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{-3}-{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/4af4a2b7389d3773cc71e843190c6ab111355248a15e6165a8e39e37252061b9.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}7{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =7\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =7(\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{{e}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-350800/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350809/field-1/13765891ebc180475a967ab52e1f8854d5842c0043a189b8d67b92f72ab25f76" :answer/id #uuid "f6748e9a-bfc9-580a-97b9-b0ca4ee46133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350809/field-1/bc5dccf24a6257467735c162ac8ff8c065c9cc47e0502e0787d3a05bb456e850" :answer/id #uuid "f36a0474-bf39-5f62-b1be-5f7138e8a915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6e^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350809/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "47c2fc38-cc18-597f-9df5-5b66fb0ac0a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350809/field-1/13765891ebc180475a967ab52e1f8854d5842c0043a189b8d67b92f72ab25f76" :answer-field/choices ["q-350809/field-1/13765891ebc180475a967ab52e1f8854d5842c0043a189b8d67b92f72ab25f76" "q-350809/field-1/bc5dccf24a6257467735c162ac8ff8c065c9cc47e0502e0787d3a05bb456e850"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350809" :question/id #uuid "b798f4b7-e5ea-58e3-9525-4ab4622494f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-350809" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}6{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}6{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2a}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{2a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{2x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{2x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{2x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/61a2aafc6dadee9e392e098f77839fdd99f3bb5d30c62cf06fef1be08c4b2682.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}6{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{2a}) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350809/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350809"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "74eb9c07-4eb1-559d-9d06-eaeb7465ee27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "f5406e24-5e2c-5e28-a011-615daf235048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "18a92478-c825-5593-96d7-1548d8d2ef3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "dc6b724a-35d2-5e47-b2fa-8ed3898fb26a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "bfeb4047-6209-56ce-84e8-a28b5b0a8ee3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8e23acf-7ccf-5757-821c-89c55aed5b9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-100378/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-100378/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-100378/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-100378/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-100378/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-100378/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-100378" :question/id #uuid "40f084aa-b80e-58f3-b339-c0f4c81b3533" :question/math-academy-id "q-100378" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}2{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{e}^{-3x}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{3a}}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{e}^{3x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{3x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{3x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/45e8ddd8ddb33dc8d6a701ed75878271b331ce6b3591ba8fae9f4fa49020c12b.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{3a}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-100378/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-100378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879/selection/f5dae69efc5c88f42f4e2a180e5667d2eb5a26fe11b4850b407f66211abb65a8" :answer/id #uuid "5e593295-571c-5135-9e5b-8082235affba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{e}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879/selection/a1a2c9254cf4541b376c718ee4aa2595e631729cb2d7ebbd92b4202d3d402d43" :answer/id #uuid "704a1e35-75a1-5a50-a1a5-b206519d97c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879/selection/0eb45dc5f5716e8a675748ab7084cb0f83b954639640cdb5407ec42c8acdb9eb" :answer/id #uuid "1f58aaa3-b2dd-5cfc-957f-ada1fd0ae91c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879/selection/80a893300e142f3132327063bc10b68ae20f5a8775c083c43524a98d513076f0" :answer/id #uuid "15d4f6c6-2675-59a6-91b8-ef0c5cb88ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879/selection/0a9854453ab5413779105a493cb62ea39bffd6b48d8813bb039953147b7a3316" :answer/id #uuid "28679009-a60a-595f-9b07-f8a6c24ee8ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9a6032-9a7d-5990-bc32-a63ae0286320" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152879/selection/0a9854453ab5413779105a493cb62ea39bffd6b48d8813bb039953147b7a3316" :answer-field/choices ["q-152879/selection/f5dae69efc5c88f42f4e2a180e5667d2eb5a26fe11b4850b407f66211abb65a8" "q-152879/selection/a1a2c9254cf4541b376c718ee4aa2595e631729cb2d7ebbd92b4202d3d402d43" "q-152879/selection/0eb45dc5f5716e8a675748ab7084cb0f83b954639640cdb5407ec42c8acdb9eb" "q-152879/selection/80a893300e142f3132327063bc10b68ae20f5a8775c083c43524a98d513076f0" "q-152879/selection/0a9854453ab5413779105a493cb62ea39bffd6b48d8813bb039953147b7a3316"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152879" :question/id #uuid "cdbc143c-1d4b-5ff7-8e96-4b65f8c9923e" :question/math-academy-id "q-152879" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{x}]}_{a}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{3}-{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{3}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/115e3198226940a76b770f5942bb06e6496bd234d6cb5fee2d33f19038931bd3.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{3}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-152879/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152879"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-350830"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4a}+\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-4x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/ade58ce56684420fb0f00236af50bbb54f76801fc8870e1cce135cbd51f1b726.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a}) \\\\  & =10(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{4}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-152875"] :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}2\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{5}^{x}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({5}^{1}-{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{5}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/06c51ecc423683f4377248004b7a318f1348836bd752a7f65f94457d1774e64d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}2\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-346615/field-1/67c038c3661b204e3dea441216d41a01fd1b794ac613f167ce4d29d1db61b899" :answer/id #uuid "a235cf02-e2f7-5789-b5b0-fa2e4829cb41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\ln(5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346615/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "30f5688f-488e-576a-a93d-3f7e26d20e2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346615/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d050717-040b-54d9-841d-e702ccee418c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346615/field-1/67c038c3661b204e3dea441216d41a01fd1b794ac613f167ce4d29d1db61b899" :answer-field/choices ["q-346615/field-1/67c038c3661b204e3dea441216d41a01fd1b794ac613f167ce4d29d1db61b899" "q-346615/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346615" :question/id #uuid "1e67e48d-05b2-55a2-b68d-67c36a777690" :question/math-academy-id "q-346615" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{5}^{x}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(5-{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{5}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/83f7d663fa66184b56c4f79d61f6e17012714a3de7512202b3022e91d4325437.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346615/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351416/field-1/4de4a3838567ec0a37f9271c483c617b01b7c052e333c412df4b3d5f0577003e" :answer/id #uuid "16d182f3-9d75-54c3-b417-f852e1ef78eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3\\ln(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351416/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b096aed0-3798-522b-84a3-5f4f8d7e125f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351416/field-1/4de4a3838567ec0a37f9271c483c617b01b7c052e333c412df4b3d5f0577003e" :answer-field/choices ["q-351416/field-1/4de4a3838567ec0a37f9271c483c617b01b7c052e333c412df4b3d5f0577003e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351416" :question/id #uuid "8db43b84-59e1-5d8b-9409-aff2fd00efef" :question/math-academy-id "q-351416" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{2}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{2}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}{2}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{2}^{3x}}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{2}^{3x}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(8-{2}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={2}^{3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{2}^{3x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{2}^{3x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/c2af905a46cea7b7512a727a5e53a2a178e4902f7114f86439365684e6685efa.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{2}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351416/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351416"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876/selection/02b2842195510c4849aa074cdb96789ffc017c113fc9b248ef69f21c1e97cb60" :answer/id #uuid "a68b6822-d4c4-57bb-ab62-e78daf46aa92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876/selection/24212cb666987ed97674ec2a8f6ed3cb14057b341efa14909e8b1e14067f5955" :answer/id #uuid "d5a478f2-f2c0-53c4-a58e-3ec9acc13f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "d5a6efce-c5a0-514c-8cb1-3b5c46335b51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876/selection/2ff68f5a05184a0e8d026345d247e350a60e8d8cd805d34a935be9dd3a1b3443" :answer/id #uuid "e90941e6-aad3-5bea-acf4-ebcf03514f21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876/selection/b5b326b687b0eea9897f23aebd11d0524f2decd380fee6604521af06decff6b4" :answer/id #uuid "5f462d65-35a6-53bb-a559-10bfba3050d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbdbf63-5e7c-5c94-95cc-df93ade79446" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152876/selection/b5b326b687b0eea9897f23aebd11d0524f2decd380fee6604521af06decff6b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-152876/selection/02b2842195510c4849aa074cdb96789ffc017c113fc9b248ef69f21c1e97cb60" "q-152876/selection/24212cb666987ed97674ec2a8f6ed3cb14057b341efa14909e8b1e14067f5955" "q-152876/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-152876/selection/2ff68f5a05184a0e8d026345d247e350a60e8d8cd805d34a935be9dd3a1b3443" "q-152876/selection/b5b326b687b0eea9897f23aebd11d0524f2decd380fee6604521af06decff6b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152876" :question/id #uuid "1cca7650-6cce-58b2-8816-dbf449a38154" :question/math-academy-id "q-152876" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}4\\cdot {6}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}4\\cdot {6}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}4\\cdot {6}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{6}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{6}^{x}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({6}^{0}-{6}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{6}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={6}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{6}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{6}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/2ebee84cf543b25e56b360f145459696554a3b67daaf64c21812cb4b92fa420a.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}4\\cdot {6}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{6}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-152876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351320/field-1/8fd9c49efbcbeec10d28a51c541600c723f64cbf4f94b3f7fac7cf72a35e0d9c" :answer/id #uuid "0945e89d-40a1-5bbd-947b-87ccb466c405" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\ln(4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351320/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa485675-6e54-5354-a5be-95b88c6790a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351320/field-1/8fd9c49efbcbeec10d28a51c541600c723f64cbf4f94b3f7fac7cf72a35e0d9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-351320/field-1/8fd9c49efbcbeec10d28a51c541600c723f64cbf4f94b3f7fac7cf72a35e0d9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351320" :question/id #uuid "0aeedd54-c10a-53bd-b367-88f50ec08852" :question/math-academy-id "q-351320" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3\\cdot {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3\\cdot {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}3\\cdot {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{3\\cdot {4}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[3\\cdot {4}^{x}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(3-3\\cdot {4}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot (3-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }3\\cdot {4}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={4}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{4}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{4}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/fd4020291b348d130fc34969d72ff683aab5b6fb95ea5f7d32b90e5245d56d9c.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3\\cdot {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot (3-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }3\\cdot {4}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot (3-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351320/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351320"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265/selection/152ff7ba5c24dc79ab618eb6f1870ec72f26d1895ca034ef79549f6a52d1d350" :answer/id #uuid "11ba0022-8ee0-5b7b-a189-37ed3554abd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" :answer/id #uuid "77087391-186d-5d91-931a-5c8ac49a7c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265/selection/0a65b2d996bdaa8617e2817a128afc8fc86ee863802c9f2a49df1b559523cd36" :answer/id #uuid "d3bd3888-4147-5cca-87d6-ef52e7d33408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265/selection/afee454593c877ba8499e80e2c829fd41fecff65f2dd92c6c5ebc0e499502713" :answer/id #uuid "f422bd08-9f0c-5578-ab9f-83881b07eecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "c8b039e2-90ed-53ae-80fa-ab83412812cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2aacc6ce-36f1-5059-9e7e-0497d1596a6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152265/selection/afee454593c877ba8499e80e2c829fd41fecff65f2dd92c6c5ebc0e499502713" :answer-field/choices ["q-152265/selection/152ff7ba5c24dc79ab618eb6f1870ec72f26d1895ca034ef79549f6a52d1d350" "q-152265/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" "q-152265/selection/0a65b2d996bdaa8617e2817a128afc8fc86ee863802c9f2a49df1b559523cd36" "q-152265/selection/afee454593c877ba8499e80e2c829fd41fecff65f2dd92c6c5ebc0e499502713" "q-152265/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152265" :question/id #uuid "30e19b72-0416-5b80-938a-cf37e67f6c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-152265" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{x}^{2}{e}^{2+{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=2+{x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2+{x}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $3$ | $-\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{x}^{2}{e}^{2+{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{x}^{2}{e}^{2+{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{3}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[{e}^{u}]_{a}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{3}-{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ({e}^{3}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{x},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/3df1853e93a5ab2a1c1ca4114d450b29a69223bd576b059d9aef1b17c68fe5b7.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{x}^{2}{e}^{2+{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ({e}^{3}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ({e}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152265/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc1fbb99-83e1-52ba-83f1-367de07351a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152265"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7b73fad5-876c-55eb-88bf-4b847cd6e4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "3114b948-3060-5b59-89f3-827cfe2524a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c4952de8-1cd2-5da5-8769-56da18627c82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "0b108031-4124-57ec-9844-c213d2e4dc23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "1331ccfd-5799-52f0-92c9-42437b8d9bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28565e4b-6627-5b45-893a-e114d620b023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-100424/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-100424/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-100424/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-100424/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-100424/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-100424/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-100424" :question/id #uuid "6c5d67b1-17eb-5fed-900a-3f60a9deeff9" :question/math-academy-id "q-100424" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{2}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-{e}^{-u}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{e}^{-u}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{a}}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/4844d6220d04a6a1fffdd5a485a9e6724aa6065397b8c3a009157a7a2dafc3cf.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-100424/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc1fbb99-83e1-52ba-83f1-367de07351a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-100424"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-100494"] :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{2}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{2}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{{2}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[{2}^{u}]_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y={2}^{a},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{2}^{a}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/b9a29cbd8a029e0f26e3da6a042ada0f8a809053233979bb4ff73db3dcf0f10d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-351529/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "264ec97b-82ef-5a8e-b277-97d6e2cf1063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351529/field-1/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer/id #uuid "1a89b222-3e93-5590-890c-fa1e2418fd5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351529/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c525b007-0a7c-5605-bc48-934795e9ca16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351529/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-351529/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-351529/field-1/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351529" :question/id #uuid "808f3d8c-e897-5a7c-8a7c-2cad7570d3cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-351529" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{5/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to {0}^{-}$ and $u\\to 0$ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=\\frac{1}{x}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{5/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{-\\infty }{e}^{5u}\\,\\text{d}u={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{5u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{5/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{e}^{5u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{e}^{5u}}{5}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{e}^{5a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{5a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{5x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{5x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{5x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/2a24352ca6421b3aa61f3f29e3c19373cca011feafce263775a2f692f67ad36b.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{5/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{5a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351529/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc1fbb99-83e1-52ba-83f1-367de07351a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "afac4dd8-6e35-5226-9687-201646535d40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257/selection/78188da1a2c8ef864843778f56881646f2ff37a1cf36feab6f80e0f0fc95c058" :answer/id #uuid "224451d0-8b48-5227-ad8c-e1aa730b4898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f47b946b-20d1-5f6d-a285-c47e250e7087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "bc20f57b-2a32-54cb-b418-754095cab358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257/selection/be7671dfcec88fd83021721c027e180f94aa5dc830cb53553598c14eaf369bc4" :answer/id #uuid "5d2e8c06-e722-5c9f-942f-f233f88a1358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a065a4c0-893c-5da3-b9da-d4021c032d1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152257/selection/be7671dfcec88fd83021721c027e180f94aa5dc830cb53553598c14eaf369bc4" :answer-field/choices ["q-152257/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-152257/selection/78188da1a2c8ef864843778f56881646f2ff37a1cf36feab6f80e0f0fc95c058" "q-152257/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-152257/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" "q-152257/selection/be7671dfcec88fd83021721c027e180f94aa5dc830cb53553598c14eaf369bc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152257" :question/id #uuid "5f999842-4b67-56b3-8661-e898a8c57652" :question/math-academy-id "q-152257" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-\\sqrt{1-x}}}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=\\sqrt{1-x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=\\sqrt{1-x}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-\\sqrt{1-x}}}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{\\infty }^{1}{e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-\\sqrt{1-x}}}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[-{e}^{-u}]_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{{e}^{a}}+\\frac{1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e}-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{a}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/4ef3194e946aec805866202a5e0ad521291d71b1fabc2df68d6cb1a4d93da42b.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-\\sqrt{1-x}}}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{e}-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{a}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-152257/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc1fbb99-83e1-52ba-83f1-367de07351a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10554"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int e^{px + q}\\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac1p e^{px+q} + C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to\\infty.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\,]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{e}^{-3x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3a}-{e}^{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=e^{-3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to -\\infty} e^{-3x} = \\infty$\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to \\infty} e^{-3x} =0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/bc4ffc41105491f2bd6b37b2482afc64946d8f67f6db83dfa322c400ae4bc2b6.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3a}-{e}^{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (0-{e}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10764"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int b^{\\,px + q}\\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac1{p\\ln(b)} b^{\\,px+q} + C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to-\\infty.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3\\cdot {2}^{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{2}^{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{2}^{2x+1}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot {2}^{1}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{2}^{2x}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({2}^{0}-{2}^{2a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{2a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=2^{2x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to -\\infty} 2^{2x} = 0$\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to \\infty} 2^{2x} = \\infty$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/009f467677932d0ac17e1632c31f4d3aa5271ffe332730d9670e69862b243bef.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3\\cdot {2}^{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{2a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10553"] :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=x^4.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 4x^3\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac 14 \\textrm{d}u =x^3\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty$ when $x\\to \\infty,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x^4$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\infty$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot {2}^{-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to\\infty.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot {2}^{-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{2}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{{2}^{-u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{2}^{-u}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{a}}-\\frac{1}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\dfrac{1}{2^x},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to -\\infty} \\dfrac{1}{2^{x}} = \\infty$\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to \\infty} \\dfrac{1}{2^{x}} = 0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/1969145d74662468ec23d458ac1ad0194d51cbf6b026718b7232466e9357efdf.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot {2}^{-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{a}}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
